[
    {
        "id": "tab-mosquitto-tls",
        "type": "tab",
        "label": "Mosquitto TLS",
        "disabled": false,
        "info": "Demo flow: listen and publish messages to the Mosquitto broker over a TLS-encrypted (mqtts) connection.\n\nBroker: mqtt:8883 (service name on the ti-dhome network) with certificate verification against the CA generated by `make certs` (/certs/ca.crt, mounted read-only in the Node-RED container).\n\nThe broker requires credentials: set the mosquitto user password in the broker node (Security tab) before deploying.\n\nUsage:\n * \"Listen test/#\" receives every message published on test/#\n * \"Publish every 10s\" publishes a timestamp on test/from-nodered\n * The listener picks up your own publications too, so the round trip is visible in the debug sidebar."
    },
    {
        "id": "comment-mosquitto-tls",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "tab-mosquitto-tls",
        "name": "Demo: MQTT over TLS (mqtts://mqtt:8883) - edit broker credentials (Security tab) and deploy",
        "info": "The broker node uses usetls with the TLS config \"Mosquitto CA\": it verifies the server certificate against /certs/ca.crt.\nRemember to fill in the Mosquitto password (user \"mosquitto\") on the Security tab of the broker node.",
        "x": 400,
        "y": 80,
        "wires": []
    },
